/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate14_nrtl_butanol_water -- THE REAL WATER + 1-BUTANOL PAIR: BUBBLE
  TEMPERATURES AND MEASURED TIE LINES IN ONE FIT (DEV.md 4c C16, C225, C226).

  The synthetic witness curate13 proves that the machinery recovers a pair it
  was given.  This case runs the same machinery (`kind T_bubble+LLE`) on
  MEASURED data from the NIST/TRC ThermoML Archive (doi 10.18434/mds2-2422,
  the copy on the curator's machine, sha256-verified), and asks the one
  question the synthetic case cannot: does an NRTL pair hold the gap the
  measurements show, its change with temperature AND the boiling liquid, and
  does it predict studies it was never handed?

  WHAT THE ARCHIVE HOLDS FOR THIS PAIR (found by reading the XML, not by the
  indexer).  No file of the archive is a pure binary water + 1-butanol study.
  Every datum below is a BINARY BLOCK inside a ternary or quaternary study (the
  authors report the binary edge of their system), so: (a) bin/choupo-thermoml
  vle-index finds ONE usable isobaric bubble series (doi 10.1021/je700411p, 15
  interior points) and the heteroazeotrope temperatures of two more; (b) the
  liquid-liquid blocks are not reached by `extract-vle`, so the tie-line files
  were written by a small curator script (kept out of the tree) that reads the
  same XML, pairs the two liquids of each temperature, and converts mass
  fractions to mole fractions (M 74.123 and 18.015 g/mol, said in the file).
  Whether a given binary row was measured by its authors or taken from the
  literature is not recorded in the archive; the files say `reviewStatus
  transcribedNotCheckedAgainstArticle` and the run announces it.

  THE PROMOTED OPERATION (C280, 2026-11-10; the sections below it are the
  negative results that led here, kept short).
  `fit_binodal` fits the BINODAL and the HETEROAZEOTROPE temperature, not the
  homogeneous butanol-rich bubble series: least squares (declared: the
  water-rich tie lines carry a 15 % scatter between laboratories, measured about
  a quadratic in T as mean 5.5 %, max 18.6 %, and a minimax objective equalises
  the largest error of both liquids at that scatter), binodal rows relative.
    FIT       bubble: 10.1016/j.jct.2014.07.021 (2 heteroazeotrope points);
              tie lines: that study and 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00302, je5007218,
              j.fluid.2007.12.003, acs.jced.6b00941 -- 14 tie lines, 288-366 K.
    HELD OUT  bubble: 10.1016/j.jct.2016.04.013 (2 heteroazeotrope points);
              29 tie lines of 21 other studies including 10.1021/je700411p.
              The homogeneous bubble series of je700411p (15 points, x 0.56-0.99,
              366-390 K) is scored by `report_homogeneous_bubble`, the SAME fit
              against that series only, so its miss is its own line and does not
              enter the heteroazeotrope verdict.  (The mixed kind needed bubble
              evidence in the fit: the two heteroazeotrope points.  Whether a
              fit with none is allowed was not tried.)
  RESULT (the engine's ERROR REPORT; five parameters b_ij 1894.0429, b_ji
  -163.8364, a_ij -4.7108, a_ji 4.0996, alpha 0.4459): VERDICT validated --
  held-out tie-line AAD 0.0056 against 0.01, held-out heteroazeotrope bubble
  0.376 K = 0.103 % against 0.23 %.  Relative error mean / max, fit | held out:
  water-rich 6.9 % / 17.3 %  |  5.2 % / 16.6 %; butanol-rich 1.9 % / 5.8 %  |
  2.2 % / 11.5 %.  Solubility of butanol in water, model: 0.0194 (288 K), 0.0175
  (320 K), 0.0173 (340 K), 0.0183 (366 K) -- the shallow minimum is drawn.
  fit_binodal_start2 lands on the same pair (b_ij 1894.08).  `fit_twoStage` (the
  fitter's default objective on this partition): b_ij 2132.88; rich-liquid
  relative 5.6 % mean, 15 % max, held-out tie-line AAD 0.0143 -- notValidated:
  minimax follows the water-rich scatter.
  WHAT THE PAIR IS NOT FOR: `report_homogeneous_bubble` scores the homogeneous
  butanol-rich series held out: mean 2.18 K = 0.59 % (max 3.2 K) against the
  0.23 % band, NOT loosened -- notValidated, as found.  The pair is for the
  liquid-liquid split and the heteroazeotrope; at 1 atm on the butanol-rich
  homogeneous side it reads about 2-3 K high.  The catalogue record says so.
  The explicit data of this section replace the "WHAT THE RUN FOUND" blocks
  below for the promoted record; those describe the earlier partition
  (je700411p in the fit, loso_* operations since dropped).

  THE FIRST PARTITION (superseded), DECLARED BEFORE THE FIRST FIT.
    FIT      bubble temperatures: doi 10.1021/je700411p (15 points, 101.3 kPa);
             tie lines: the five studies that report THREE OR MORE
             temperatures -- 10.1021/je700411p (5), 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00302 (3),
             10.1021/je5007218 (3), 10.1016/j.fluid.2007.12.003 (3),
             10.1021/acs.jced.6b00941 (3): 17 tie lines, 288-362 K.
    HELD OUT bubble temperatures: 10.1016/j.jct.2014.07.021 and
             10.1016/j.jct.2016.04.013 (two heteroazeotrope temperatures each,
             about 365.8 K); tie lines: the eighteen other studies, one or
             two temperatures each (21 tie lines, 288-366 K).  No author name
             of a held-out study appears in a fit study (the archive carries no
             affiliations, so a shared author is the dependence the rule can
             check).
    BANDS    written in `acceptance` below with their origin (maxAAD 0.23 % of
             T, maxLLE 0.01 in mole fraction).
    TRIAGE   `loso_*` fit the pair with ONE tie-line study moved from fit to
             held-out in turn, to see whether the verdict is the property of
             the pair or of one study.

  OBJECTIVE (C280).  The operations below run the DEFAULT objective of
  `fitParameters`, twoStage, with tie-line rows relative; read the run header for
  the one that produced a number.  The weights stated under THE FIT are the
  pre-C280 ones: the tie-line weight is now `sigmaRelative`, below.
  THE FIT.  NRTL with tau_ij = a_ij + b_ij/T and alpha free: FIVE parameters
  (b_ij, b_ji, a_ij, a_ji, alpha), i = nButanol, j = water.  Bubble rows are
  weighted by 1/U (each point's own stated expanded uncertainty), tie-line mole
  fractions by 1/0.0005.  The start (b_ij 0, b_ji 1000 K, a 0, alpha 0.30)
  splits the liquid at every measured tie line; `fit_mixed_start2` starts
  elsewhere (400 / 1400 / alpha 0.40) and must land on the same pair.

  THE FIRST FORM, AND WHY IT WAS LEFT (kept as the record of a negative
  result).  With a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30 fixed and the tie lines weighted
  by 1/0.005, the fit gave b_ij = -39.14 K, b_ji = 1178.21 K: held-out bubble
  AAD 1.72 K, held-out tie-line AAD 0.0165, and a butanol solubility in water
  that ROSE from 0.019 (288 K) to 0.067 (366 K) where the measurements keep it
  flat (0.016-0.021).  Two b's and one alpha cannot draw a flat solubility
  line, and a weight of 0.005 on a mole fraction of 0.02 cannot see it.  Both
  were changed, each with its reason in `residual` and `acceptance` below; the
  tie-line band (0.01) was not.

  WHAT THE ABSOLUTE LEAST-SQUARES RUN FOUND -- the form this case had before
  C280 (measured, not argued; reproduced 2026-11-10 by `objective { method
  leastSquares; scale { binodal absolute; } }` with `liquidLiquid { sigma
  0.0005; }`, the numbers below to the last digit).  VALIDATED under the bands
  below.  It is NO LONGER what `expected` pins: the case now runs the default
  objective, and the section "WHAT THE MINIMAX STAGE FOUND" below says what that
  gave.
    * fit_mixed: b_ij = 1486.66 K, b_ji = -27.30 K, a_ij = -3.6282,
      a_ji = 3.6295, alpha = 0.4428; fit_mixed_start2 lands on the same five
      numbers.  The four tau parameters are strongly correlated (max|corr|
      0.998, cond JtJ 3.5e4): the pair is ONE set, to be used whole, and no
      single number of it carries a meaning.
    * Solubility of butanol in water (mole fraction, model): 0.0188 at 288 K,
      0.0186 at 300 K, 0.0189 at 320 K, 0.0197 at 340 K, 0.0215 at 366 K --
      flat, as measured.  HELD OUT (21 tie lines, 18 studies, all predicted as
      two liquids): AAD 0.0061 against 0.01; water-rich liquid AAD 0.0010 (max
      0.0027), butanol-rich liquid AAD 0.0113 (max 0.060, recomputed outside
      the engine).  The largest miss is one measurement, x = 0.550 at 298.15 K
      (10.1016/j.fluid.2014.07.011), where two other studies report 0.487 and
      0.488 at the same temperature and the model gives 0.490.  In the fit set
      the largest tie-line miss is 0.021.
    * Bubble temperatures HELD OUT (4 heteroazeotrope points, two studies):
      AAD 0.53 K = 0.15 % against 0.23 %.
    * Leave-one-study-out (4 of the 5 tie-line fit studies; the fifth,
      10.1021/je700411p, is the only bubble series and the engine refuses its
      archive file in both roles): alpha 0.4385-0.4456, held-out tie-line AAD
      0.0029-0.0075, held-out bubble AAD 0.54-0.59 K; every verdict is the
      same.  The result is the pair's against these data, not one study's.
    * IN RELATIVE TERMS (recomputed outside the engine), which is how a
      composition is judged: butanol-rich liquid, mean 1.1 % (max 4.0 %) in the
      fit set and 2.3 % (max 10.9 %, the one 298.15 K point above) held out;
      water-rich liquid, mean 12 % (max 24 %) in the fit set and 5.5 % (max
      17 %) held out.  The studies themselves disagree by that much on the
      water-rich liquid (0.0159 to 0.0207 at 298.15 K, 0.0170 to 0.0220 at
      303 K), and below 320 K the model runs through the middle of them.
      ABOVE 320 K IT IS SYSTEMATICALLY HIGH, 0.019-0.021 against 0.016-0.019:
      the shallow minimum the measurements show near 333 K is not drawn.
    * WHAT THE MINIMAX STAGE FOUND (C280; the default objective, twoStage, binodal
      rows RELATIVE with `sigmaRelative 0.025` -- the absolute 0.0005 expressed at
      the water-rich liquid's mole fraction of 0.02 -- and bubble rows absolute
      in kelvin at 1/U; 49 rows: 15 bubble, 34 tie-line; 27 s for the six operations).  The
      practice Vitor asked for (2026-11-10): least squares for the first
      estimate, then minimise the LARGEST scaled error.  VERDICT: notValidated,
      reported as found and with no band, weight or bound changed to reach
      another one: held-out tie-line AAD 0.0186 against the 0.01 band (bubble
      AAD 0.21 % = 0.77 K, inside 0.23 %).  Relative mean / max error, fit set |
      held-out set:
                                    fit set            held out
                                  mean     max       mean     max
        water-rich liquid         6.7 %   15.7 %     6.7 %   19.2 %
        butanol-rich liquid       5.7 %   15.7 %     7.8 %   17.2 %
        bubble T (absolute)    0.60 K  1.07 K      0.77 K  0.96 K
      against the pre-C280 pair: water-rich 12 % / 24 % fit and 5.4 % / 17 %
      held out; butanol-rich 1.1 % / 4.0 % and 2.3 % / 10.9 %; bubble T fit mean
      2.1 K, max 3.1 K.  Solubility of butanol in water, model (mole fraction),
      measured 0.016-0.021 below 320 K and 0.016-0.019 above:
                       288 K    320 K    340 K    366 K
        pre-C280       0.0188   0.0189   0.0197   0.0215   (rises above 320 K)
        stage 1 (LS)   0.0191   0.0174   0.0171   0.0174
        minimax        0.0197   0.0179   0.0175   0.0176   (flat, in the band)
      (outside the engine: NRTL, equal activities, from the printed parameters.)
      What it means: the systematic 15 % excess of the water-rich liquid above
      320 K is gone, and the largest relative miss of the fit set fell from 24 %
      to 15.7 %.  The price is on the OTHER liquid: the relative scale lets a
      mole fraction of 0.5 miss by 15 % -- 0.07 -- as the 0.02 one does, so the
      butanol-rich side went from AAD 0.011 to 0.036 held out and the verdict
      flipped on the binodal band, which is absolute.  The stage-1 (relative
      least-squares) pair alone gives held-out tie-line AAD 0.0136, also
      above 0.01.  Three things the run also showed: (a) the minimax objective
      equalises the relative errors of both liquids at the scatter level of the
      water-rich measurements (15 %, the between-study scatter), which the
      butanol-rich liquid does not have; a per-property weight, or a bound
      below the data's own scatter, is the lever -- not changed here; (b)
      the maximum is not smooth, and `fit_mixed_start2` ends at a different
      point (b_ij 1790 against 1680) where stage 1 alone lands on the same pair
      from both starts (1684.63 / 1684.64); (c) the correlation is 1.000 at the
      reported point, so the four tau numbers are still one set.  The pair is
      NOT promoted.
    * Independence: je700411p supplies the bubble series AND five tie lines of
      the fit (the run announces "one publication, counted twice"); the five
      held-out heteroazeotrope temperatures are three values (365.7-366.2 K).

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair lives in this frame: ideal-gas vapour, the
  catalogue's Antoine records (water 0.70 K low at 1 atm, C226 item 7),
  one pressure for the bubble data (101.3 kPa), LLE data at about atmospheric
  pressure.  Nothing here tests it at another pressure or with another vapour
  model.
